# .claudeheavy — token landmines
#
# Files that are legitimate to work with, but whose WHOLE-FILE Read costs so
# many tokens it damages the session. Read/Edit/Write are blocked here;
# **Grep is deliberately allowed**, because grep returns only matching lines.
# Bash and the Python scripts are untouched.
#
# This is not a "do not touch" list. It is a "do not slurp" list: every entry
# has a cheaper canonical access path, named below.
#
# Enforced by .claude/hooks/check-claudeignore.sh (second tier).
# Measured by `make context-budget` (metric M2).

# ── Generated PCB / schematic sources ───────────────────────────────
# ~265k tokens each. Canonical access: scripts/pcb_cache.py load_cache(),
# which parses pads/vias/segments/zones into JSON with SHA-256 invalidation.
# These files are GENERATED by scripts/generate_pcb/ — edit the generator.
*.kicad_pcb
hardware/kicad/*.kicad_sch

# ── Generated schematic renders ─────────────────────────────────────
# 96k-250k tokens each of path data. Look at the PNG renders instead, or
# regenerate with `make render-schematics`.
website/static/img/schematics/*.svg

# ── Emulator core: generated tables ─────────────────────────────────
# 100k-313k tokens each of machine-generated dispatch / cycle-count /
# ROM-database tables. Nothing in them is hand-written or reviewable;
# grep for the one opcode or ROM entry you need.
software/components/gwenesis/cpus/M68K/m68ki_instruction_jump_table*.h
software/components/gwenesis/cpus/M68K/m68kops.h
software/components/gwenesis/cpus/M68K/m68ki_cycles*.h
software/components/nofrendo/database.h

# ── Generated PCB renders ───────────────────────────────────────────
# 32k-52k tokens of path data. Use the PNG renders in the same folders.
website/static/img/pcb/*.svg
release_jlcpcb/renders/*.svg

# ── Audit history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2442 lines / ~38k tokens covering audit rounds R1-R9, overwhelmingly
# CLOSED findings. This is history: grep it for a specific R#-CRIT-# id
# when tracing why something is the way it is. Current open items live in
# the memory index, not here.
hardware-audit-bugs.md

# ── Dependency lockfiles ────────────────────────────────────────────
# 184k tokens. Use `npm ls <pkg>` or grep for the one package you care about.
package-lock.json

# ── Interactive BOM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single-file HTML with the whole board embedded as JSON. Regenerated by the
# stop-regen-ibom hook; never read or hand-edit.
website/static/ibom/ibom.html

# ── External DFM reports ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~64k tokens each of KiCad-generated HTML tables. Written by
# scripts/external-dfm.sh; grep for the violation id, or read the summary the
# script prints. Editing them changes nothing — rerun the script.
hardware/kicad/external-dfm-output/*.html

# ── Net Explorer data ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~77k tokens: every net, pad and track of the board as JSON. GENERATED by
# scripts/generate_net_explorer.py (`make net-explorer`), and
# verify_net_explorer_fresh gates its staleness. To answer a question about a
# net, use scripts/pcb_cache.py load_cache() or the viewer page itself.
website/static/net-explorer-data.json

# ── Parsed PCB cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~31k tokens. This file IS the cheap access path to the .kicad_pcb — but only
# through its API. Call load_cache() from scripts/pcb_cache.py, which returns
# the parsed dict and handles SHA-256 invalidation; slurping the raw JSON
# spends a third of the cost the cache exists to avoid. Never hand-edit: it is
# rebuilt from the board whenever the hash changes.
hardware/kicad/.pcb_cache.json

# ── Generated reports ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~103k tokens. Canonical access: `python3 scripts/erc_check.py` prints the
# classified summary; `--run` regenerates. Grep for a specific violation.
hardware/kicad/.erc-report.json

# ~130k tokens across drc/erc JSON once KiBot's ERC phase started working
# (2026-07-31). Canonical access: the summary scripts/external-dfm.sh
# prints, or `python3 scripts/verify_erc.py` for the gated view; grep the
# JSON for one violation id if needed.
hardware/kicad/external-dfm-output/*.json
hardware/kicad/external-dfm-output/kibot.log

# ── Vendored emulator cores (third-party) ───────────────────────────
# snes9x / smsplus / nofrendo sources, 25-36k tokens per file. Not ours:
# upstream is the reference. Canonical access: grep for the symbol you
# need; edits are rare and go through Bash heredoc/sed.
software/components/

# ESP-IDF managed dependencies (downloaded by idf component manager,
# gitignored — the ESP-IDF equivalent of node_modules). Contains 170k-token
# generated image .c files. Never edit: pin versions in idf_component.yml.
software/managed_components/

# ── Audit log ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~47k tokens of append-only history. Canonical access: grep a finding id
# (R25-CRIT-1) or a round header; append new rounds with Bash heredoc.
hardware-audit-bugs.md
